      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T07:56:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean, the fragment is implemented by vendor bt usb driver.\nFor example:\nIf MTU in Read Buffer Size Complete events is 100 + 3. MTU in usb sco ep is 20 + 3.\nStack can send sco packet with length 103. Vendor bt usb driver will fragment this packet to 5 packets with length (20 + 3) * 5.\nStack receive the sco packet with length 20 + 3 only from vendor bt driver.\nIt works well\n\nBut for VTS, VTS send sco packet with length 103 and vendor bt usb driver will fragment it. After loopback, VTS will receive 5 packets with length 20 + 3. VTS will check failed.\n\nThat\u0027s why I submit this patch. Let VTS only send the packet that can\u0027t not be fragmented.\n\nMTU in usb sco ep is a usb feature only. So I think that the fragment is implemented by vendor bt usb driver is a good solution",
      "parentUuid": "4bfab077_8815a6f0",
      "revId": "07ae05e1d28820f454f52f729059990fc9fb00b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
